# 必考词 Unit15
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit15核心高频词汇

{{monitor}}{/ˈmɒnɪtər/}}{v. 监控；n. 显示器}}{{The system monitors air quality in real time.}}

{{moral}}{/ˈmɒrəl/}}{adj. 道德的；n. 寓意}}{{The story teaches an important moral lesson.}}

{{moreover}}{/mɔːrˈəʊvər/}}{adv. 此外；而且}}{{The plan is effective; moreover, it is cost-efficient.}}

{{motive}}{/ˈməʊtɪv/}}{n. 动机；目的}}{{The police are investigating the motive behind the crime.}}

{{multiple}}{/ˈmʌltɪpl/}}{adj. 多重的；多个的}}{{She has multiple talents including singing and painting.}}

{{mutual}}{/ˈmjuːtʃuəl/}}{adj. 相互的；共同的}}{{The agreement was based on mutual respect and trust.}}

{{mystery}}{/ˈmɪstri/}}{n. 神秘；谜}}{{The disappearance of the plane remains a mystery.}}

{{narrative}}{/ˈnærətɪv/}}{n. 叙述；故事}}{{The novel has a compelling narrative that keeps readers engaged.}}

{{narrow}}{/ˈnærəʊ/}}{adj. 狭窄的；v. 缩小}}{{The path was too narrow for two people to walk side by side.}}

{{nation}}{/ˈneɪʃn/}}{n. 国家；民族}}{{The nation celebrated its independence day with fireworks.}}

{{negative}}{/ˈneɡətɪv/}}{adj. 消极的；否定的}}{{Try to turn negative experiences into learning opportunities.}}

{{neglect}}{/nɪˈɡlekt/}}{v./n. 忽视；疏忽}}{{Do not neglect your health while pursuing your career.}}

{{negotiate}}{/nɪˈɡəʊʃieɪt/}}{v. 谈判；协商}}{{The unions negotiated better working conditions for employees.}}

{{nevertheless}}{/ˌnevəðəˈles/}}{adv. 然而；不过}}{{The task was difficult; nevertheless, they completed it on time.}}

{{neutral}}{/ˈnjuːtrəl/}}{adj. 中立的；中性的}}{{Switzerland remained neutral during the two world wars.}}

{{norm}}{/nɔːrm/}}{n. 标准；规范}}{{Social norms vary greatly from one culture to another.}}

{{notable}}{/ˈnəʊtəbl/}}{adj. 值得注意的；显著的}}{{There has been a notable improvement in air quality.}}

{{notion}}{/ˈnəʊʃn/}}{n. 概念；想法}}{{The notion that money can buy happiness is debatable.}}

{{novel}}{/ˈnɒvl/}}{adj. 新颖的；n. 小说}}{{The scientist proposed a novel approach to the problem.}}

{{nuclear}}{/ˈnjuːkliər/}}{adj. 核的；原子能的}}{{Nuclear energy is a controversial topic in environmental debates.}}

{{numerous}}{/ˈnjuːmərəs/}}{adj. 众多的；许多的}}{{Numerous studies have shown the benefits of exercise.}}

{{nutrition}}{/njuːˈtrɪʃn/}}{n. 营养}}{{Good nutrition is essential for healthy development.}}

{{obey}}{/əˈbeɪ/}}{v. 服从；遵守}}{{Citizens are expected to obey the law.}}

{{objective}}{/əbˈdʒektɪv/}}{n. 目标；adj. 客观的}}{{The main objective of the study is to find a cure.}}

{{obligation}}{/ˌɒblɪˈɡeɪʃn/}}{n. 义务；责任}}{{Paying taxes is a legal obligation for all citizens.}}

{{observe}}{/əbˈzɜːrv/}}{v. 观察；遵守}}{{Scientists observed the behavior of the animals in the wild.}}

{{obstacle}}{/ˈɒbstəkl/}}{n. 障碍；阻碍}}{{Lack of funding is a major obstacle to the project.}}

{{obtain}}{/əbˈteɪn/}}{v. 获得；得到}}{{She obtained a degree in engineering from a top university.}}

{{obvious}}{/ˈɒbviəs/}}{adj. 明显的；显而易见的}}{{The answer to the question is obvious to everyone.}}

{{occupy}}{/ˈɒkjupaɪ/}}{v. 占据；使忙碌}}{{The meeting occupied most of the morning.}}

{{occur}}{/əˈkɜːr/}}{v. 发生；出现}}{{Accidents are more likely to occur in bad weather.}}

{{offend}}{/əˈfend/}}{v. 冒犯；犯罪}}{{I did not mean to offend you with my remarks.}}

{{operate}}{/ˈɒpəreɪt/}}{v. 操作；经营；动手术}}{{The surgeon operated on the patient for three hours.}}

{{opponent}}{/əˈpəʊnənt/}}{n. 对手；反对者}}{{The chess player defeated his opponent in the final round.}}

{{opportunity}}{/ˌɒpəˈtjuːnəti/}}{n. 机会}}{{The internship provides a great opportunity to gain experience.}}

{{oppose}}{/əˈpəʊz/}}{v. 反对；对抗}}{{Many citizens opposed the construction of the new highway.}}

{{optimistic}}{/ˌɒptɪˈmɪstɪk/}}{adj. 乐观的}}{{She remains optimistic about the future of the economy.}}

{{option}}{/ˈɒpʃn/}}{n. 选择；选项}}{{We have several options to choose from.}}

{{orient}}{/ˈɔːrient/}}{v. 使适应；定向}}{{The program helps new students orient themselves to campus life.}}

{{origin}}{/ˈɒrɪdʒɪn/}}{n. 起源；出身}}{{The origin of the tradition dates back centuries.}}
